A||||6||Dan||Polygraphite bushings||||1||
Z||000000||Dan||02-19-2000||09:24 AM|||| I am looking for a supplier for rear control arm polygraphite bushings.Anyone have any leads or part numbers?I want to use polygraphite to eliminate squeaking.Does anyone else desire to install the polygraphite bushings?Perhaps if I can show a market, perhaps PST or someone will match up a kit for Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-19-2000||11:22 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-19-2000||11:29 AM||||I bought my poly bushings from them, they have great prices. But, last I heard though, they don't stock the graphite impregnated control bushings for Fieros, but they do have the sway bar kits in polygraphite.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||02-19-2000||08:09 PM||||Heres a thought:  Mix dry graphite into the silicone poly bushing lube and use it as normal.  Although the silicon does not last for a long period, it would leave behind the graphite, which does!  The lock lube found in any parts store is an excellent source for graphite of the desired quality.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||02-19-2000||10:51 PM||||Mike, that sound like a good idea. It's too late for me to try your method on my front end, but I still have the rear control arm bushings to do, I might just try your suggestion when I do them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||02-20-2000||06:22 AM||||I don't have any poly bushings but I did have my garage door spring replaced. So what you say!! Let me tell ya, the guy gave me a can of spray penetrating grease which I have been using for all sorts of things. It really gets grease into all kinds of nooks and crannies. It penetrates like WD 40 but leaves a grease film behind, might be just the ticket for squeaky bushings.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phaeton||02-20-2000||01:39 PM||||Sounds suspiciously like open chain lube, penetrating oil carries nonsticky lube to the inner rollers and leaves it there, plugging the gap it entered through.  Available at motorcycle shops and belt conveyer supply houses.<BR>I abuse it as a GP lube but never thought to spray it on Fiero parts, thank you Phil.||||reg||14
